-{"attempts":0,"blocked_reason":null,"blocked_since":null,"blocks":["TJ-GAP-056"],"capability_tags":["security","cli","namespaces"],"ci_result":"GREEN","commit_hash":"505315a","completed_at":"2026-09-18T12:16:00Z","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-09-16 05:47:30","depends_on":null,"detail":"Two known gaps of the unshare-only backend, both fixed for free by bwrap: (1) unshare --pid without --mount-proc leaves the HOST /proc visible inside the jail (own docs: 'host PID view exposed') — bwrap bind-mounts a fresh procfs so jailed processes cannot enumerate host PIDs; (2) orphaned jails when the wrapper dies — bwrap --die-with-parent is a kernel-guaranteed cleanup. bwrap is the same kernel primitives, purpose-built (flatpak lineage), and already present on karaHermes (/usr/bin/bwrap 0.11.1) and kara-lair (/usr/bin/bwrap). Scope: standalone/terminal-jail learns a backend selector: TERMINAL_JAIL_JAIL_BACKEND=auto|bwrap|unshare (default auto: bwrap when present on PATH, else unshare). Same CLI surface, same verdict path, same exit-code contract (fail-closed 2/126 semantics unchanged). Do NOT change the interruptor or any Python engine rule.","dispatched_at":null,"exit_code":null,"fallback_model":null,"fallback_provider":null,"files_changed":null,"foreman_note":"Worker glm-5.3-flash @ zai-glm-default. CI run 35343596380 is green on 505315a. Initial GitReins Tier 1 used Python 3.10 and hit missing tomllib; independent repository .venv Python 3.11 full suite passed.","guard_result":"PASS","id":"TJ-GAP-054","lines_added":0,"lines_removed":0,"primary_model":"glm-5.3-flash","primary_provider":"zai-glm-default","priority":"P0","reasoning":"Bane design question 2026-09-16 (unshare vs bubblewrap): both need unprivileged user namespaces, so AppArmor-restricted hosts stay DEGRADED under either; the win is a private /proc and guaranteed jail teardown. Wrapper-layer change only — the wrapper already execs a jail command. bwrap variant must keep --unshare-user/--unshare-pid semantics equ